// Markdown's share of the lint contract. `npm run lint:md`, and a step in the
// `static` CI job beside format/lint/typecheck/proto.
//
// **The default ruleset is unusable here and that is a fact about this repo,
// not about markdownlint.** Measured across the 77 tracked docs before any
// config existed, AT THE COMMIT THIS FILE WAS ADDED: 2178 findings, of which
// 2164 were MD013/line-length at the default 80 columns — 99.4%.
// `rdm-spec.md` alone carried 715 of those (717 findings in that file, the
// other two being the `<br>` pair below). The house style
// puts a full paragraph in a table cell, so every prose doc fails that rule by
// construction, and a signal-to-noise ratio of 1-in-155 is not a lint run
// anybody reads.
//
// The 14 that were left are what this exists to keep at zero: 8 unlabelled code
// fences (fixed — they were ASCII diagrams and state machines, now `text`), 4
// on the generated ERDs (exempted below, next to the files), and 2 deliberate
// `<br>` tags.
//
// **This is the only place those figures live.** They are a snapshot, not a
// number anything regenerates — re-derive them and you get 2170, because the 8
// fences are fixed, and it moves again with the next doc added. `ci.yml` used
// to carry a second copy; ADR 0039's twenty-six-that-was-twenty-four is what
// one prose count in several places does.
//
// To re-derive: BOTH configs have to move aside, this one and
// `docs/reference/erd/.markdownlint.json`. cli2 auto-loads and merges every
// config it finds, so moving only this one leaves the ERD exemption in force
// and reports 2166 with zero MD041 rather than 2170 with four.
{
  // `.gitignore` already excludes `node_modules`, every `.venv` and
  // `docs/archive` — the archive being the point, since it is personal working
  // material rather than published documentation. Reusing that list beats a
  // second `ignores` array that would drift from it.
  "gitignore": true,
  "globs": ["**/*.md"],
  "config": {
    // **Off, not widened.** A larger limit would still be arbitrary and would
    // still fail every table, because a cell holding a sentence cannot wrap —
    // markdown tables have no continuation line. The alternative markdownlint
    // offers, `tables: false`, does not help either: measured, the prose
    // paragraphs outside tables break it too, since this repo writes long
    // sentences on one line and lets the renderer wrap them.
    //
    // Nothing is lost that another tool covers: prettier already governs
    // formatting for the files it globs, and it does not reflow markdown prose.
    "MD013": false,

    // `<br>` inside a table cell, twice in `rdm-spec.md`. There is no markdown
    // spelling for a line break in a table — the pipe syntax has no
    // continuation — so the tag is the only way to express it and banning it
    // would mean losing the break, not writing it differently.
    "MD033": { "allowed_elements": ["br"] },

    // MD041 is NOT disabled here. It is switched off only for
    // `docs/reference/erd/`, in that directory's own config, so a hand-written
    // doc still has to open with a heading.
  },
}
